Approach: Use HashMap to store value → index. For each element, check if (target - nums[i]) exists; if yes, return indices.

Time Complexity: O(n) — single pass through array, and each HashMap lookup takes O(1) on average.

Space Complexity: O(n) — storing up to n elements in the HashMap.

class Solution {
    public int[] twoSum(int[] nums, int target) {
        int n=nums.length;
        Map<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            int val=target-nums[i];
            if(!map.containsKey(val)){
                map.put(nums[i],i);
            }else{
                return new int[]{map.get(val),i};
            }
        }
        return new int[]{-1,-1};
